1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Goddamn little...

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,940
Mom?

3
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,040
Kaio!

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,540
You little shit, where the hell have you been?

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:19,540
I'll shoot!

6
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,900
I should have known.

7
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:25,680
This was all you're doing, wasn't it?

8
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,280
Who the hell do you think you are hiding my kid from me?

9
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,420
I damn near lost my mind worrying.

10
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:32,580
I'm gonna sue the shit out of you for this!

11
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:35,960
She's been gone three days.

12
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:38,840
In all that time, did you even bother looking for her?

13
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:39,640
Wait, what?

14
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:41,500
Are you...

15
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,140
So now I'm the bad guy?

16
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:46,000
You goddamn bitch!

17
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:47,500
I'll kill you!

18
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:57,920
Kaio!

19
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,180
Let go of me!

20
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:01,020
You didn't worry about her.

21
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:04,660
The only person you were worrying about was yourself.

22
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:05,340
What?

23
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:05,920
Do you know what?

24
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:09,560
I'm the bad guy.

25
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:11,860
Love to be best!

26
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:41,840
作詞・作曲・編曲 初音ミク

27
00:01:41,860 --> 00:02:11,840
作曲・編曲 初音ミク

28
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:41,840
作曲・編曲 初音ミク

29
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:45,780
Dammit, Kyle! They're calling me right now!

30
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:46,740
You hear me?

31
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,780
Talking to you, you little retard!

32
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:50,980
Miss Hinazuki, that's enough.

33
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:54,600
Do you think it's fun for her seeing you act like this?

34
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:55,580
That's your fault!

35
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:58,120
You called me a piece of shit mom in front of my daughter!

36
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:01,400
Who the hell do you think you are, taking people's kids away?

37
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:02,660
Shut up!

38
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:05,160
You're the one that beats her and throws her in sheds.

39
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:07,700
She's been gone three days and you've done jack shit!

40
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:11,480
I'm not going to stand here and get lectured by you, you brat.

41
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:13,680
You don't know what being a pair is like!

42
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,680
Get out of here, you!

43
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:18,540
Ms. Inazuki!

44
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:22,760
We're with the Department of Child Protective Services.

45
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:23,760
Huh?

46
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:26,020
We'd like to speak to you about your daughter.

47
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:28,660
Now we can do this the easy way or the hard way.

48
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:29,500
It's up to you.

49
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:33,660
Goddamn the both of you.

50
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:34,920
You tricked me.

51
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:37,920
Don't blame Ms. Fuji-numa.

52
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,800
She's here because we asked her.

53
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:43,340
You've been avoiding us, so we really didn't have any other choice.

54
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:44,140
I what?

55
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:45,960
I wasn't avoiding you!

56
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:47,880
Regardless, we're here now.

57
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:50,740
Thank you.

58
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:52,960
I'm sorry to have to drag you into this.

59
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,120
No, you don't have to be.

60
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:58,380
There were a couple things I wanted to say to her myself.

61
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:00,780
I'm glad you gave me the opportunity to.

62
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:03,700
Last I checked, kidnapping someone's kid was still illegal.

63
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:05,580
You gonna call the cops or what?

64
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,180
No.

65
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:10,220
We're not calling anyone until we've had a chance to speak to you about your daughter's welfare.

66
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:10,920
Huh?

67
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,320
What are you talking about?

68
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,960
Now that she's back home with me, she'll be fine.

69
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:18,960
Based on the facts at hand, I'm afraid we'll have to take custody of her.

70
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:19,500
What?

71
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:21,300
I'm her mother, you asshole!

72
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:25,000
Like the boy said, she was gone for three days and you didn't look for her.

73
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:26,320
What, are you denying that?

74
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:27,380
That son of a...

75
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:28,880
He's the one who took her!

76
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:30,200
What are you people nuts?

77
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,540
I'm not the criminal here!

78
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,840
Miss Inazuki, please.

79
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,660
Let's talk calmly about this.

80
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:35,120
Okay.

81
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:37,640
Let's all go talk to the cops.

82
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:38,300
What?

83
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:39,200
You heard me.

84
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,320
They can settle this.

85
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:41,460
Come on, Kaio.

86
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:43,580
Wait, hold on.

87
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,060
Calm down.

88
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:44,860
Miss Inazuki.

89
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:46,500
You're not helping your daughter.

90
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,100
Where are you going?

91
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:49,240
God damn it.

92
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:50,440
Stop dragging your feet.

93
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:53,960
Kaio, move it, you little...

94
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:54,440
Akimi!

95
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:00,080
Akimi?

96
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:03,120
Mom?

97
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:09,540
I'm so sorry.

98
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:16,020
It's my fault we haven't spoken since I made you leave that man.

99
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:20,560
And ever since, I've been worrying about you and Kaio.

100
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:25,440
I know what it's like trying to raise a kid all by yourself.

101
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,400
All the sacrifices you have to make.

102
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:31,900
It must have been tough for you.

103
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:33,380
And lonely, too.

104
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,900
I should have taken you both in and helped you.

105
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:48,760
You had to deal with so much.

106
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:51,120
I should have been there for you.

107
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:11,300
Please don't blame her.

108
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,760
This is my fault.

109
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,420
If I was around, this wouldn't have happened.

110
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:24,340
Mom.

111
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:27,280
Mom.

112
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:35,080
I wasn't buying it.

113
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:37,420
If anything, she felt sorry for herself.

114
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:43,140
Kaio wasn't buying any of it, either.

115
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,140
She wouldn't even look at her mom.

116
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:46,520
I don't blame her.

117
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:48,240
Akimi?

118
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:51,140
Don't you worry about Kaio now.

119
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:54,900
I promise you, I'll take good care of her.

120
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:57,620
I can't imagine what you're going through.

121
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,840
My child's the most precious thing I have.

122
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,480
He's my everything, and I know Kaio is yours.

123
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:11,140
Thanks, Mr. Yashiro.

124
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:11,660
No.

125
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:15,660
The reason we're all here is because of you, Satoru.

126
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:19,200
After everything you've done, and all the courage you've shown,

127
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:20,900
this couldn't have ended any better.

128
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,960
Thanks to you, she's alive.

129
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:28,700
I can barely remember my dad.

130
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:32,540
I wonder if he was anything like Mr. Yashiro.

131
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:38,180
Thank you, Satoru.

132
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:41,720
You got me out of this nightmare.

133
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,620
Kaio, ready?

134
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:56,360
The Town Without Me, by Kaio Hinazuki.

135
00:07:57,260 --> 00:08:00,980
When I get bigger, big enough to go somewhere by myself,

136
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:04,440
I want to go someplace far away from here.

137
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,100
I want to go to an island.

138
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:09,800
An island without any people.

139
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:14,140
An island that doesn't have any pain or sadness on it, either.

140
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:24,120
When I feel like I want to climb a tree, I can climb it.

141
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:29,080
I'll go for a swim if I want to, and sleep when I want to.

142
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,560
And when I think about the town without me,

143
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:41,040
I feel relief more than anything.

144
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:45,120
All I want is to go far away.

145
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:02,160
I did it.

146
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:03,700
I saved Kaio.

147
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:06,640
I changed things so she could have a future.

148
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:11,520
Now she has a chance to grow up to be whatever she wants to be.

149
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:14,140
She's on her way.

150
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:17,040
And I have a feeling she's going to be just fine.

151
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:25,420
Is he okay?

152
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:27,660
He's been like this ever since Kaio left.

153
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:29,360
He's in hibernation mode.

154
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,480
Being a superhero takes a lot out of a guy.

155
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,560
Hey, Satoru.

156
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:34,960
Are you okay?

157
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:35,960
Yeah.

158
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:37,000
Great.

159
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,460
I don't know, dude.

160
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:39,400
You don't look it.

161
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:40,760
Jeez, can you blame him?

162
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,780
I mean, his girlfriend moved to another town.

163
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:46,080
Well, the important thing is, she's safe now.

164
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,760
Satoru, can I see you for a sec?

165
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,060
I have some news.

166
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:55,320
Kaio's grandmother has full custody of her now.

167
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:57,260
And as for Kaio's mother,

168
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,760
the authorities aren't going to let her see her for a while.

169
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:02,040
Thank you, Mr. Yashiro.

170
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:04,440
Well, you deserve to know.

171
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,600
It's not about that.

172
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:09,240
You said it couldn't have ended any better

173
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:11,320
after what I did and the courage I showed.

174
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:14,560
I just wanted to let you know that meant a lot to me.

175
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,340
Well, actually,

176
00:10:17,900 --> 00:10:20,780
I wanted to say you deserve to be rewarded for your courage,

177
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,200
but that would have sounded awful.

178
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:24,260
Not that you shouldn't be rewarded,

179
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:26,660
because if anyone deserves to be, it's you.

180
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:31,040
I bet seeing Kaio's smile was your reward, wasn't it?

181
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:37,180
Your smile was mine.

182
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,280
Oh, by the way,

183
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,420
where was Kaio staying?

184
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,200
At your house?

185
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:43,600
No, not there.

186
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:44,600
We hit her.

187
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:45,280
Seriously?

188
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:46,000
Yep.

189
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,900
We set her up in this old bus

190
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:50,240
Izumi Elementary's hockey club used to use.

191
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:50,840
Huh.

192
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,500
I guess if you want to kidnap someone,

193
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,100
that's a perfect place to take him, huh?

194
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:56,160
I guess.

195
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,480
If he only knew.

196
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:02,560
Even though Kaio's safe now,

197
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:05,280
Aya, Nakanishi, and Hiromi are still in danger.

198
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:08,160
I have to figure out a way to make sure

199
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,500
neither of them are left alone.

200
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:14,680
Like how I did with Kaio.

201
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:19,520
Hiromi's my friend, and I'm with him all the time.

202
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:21,500
But Aya goes to a different school,

203
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:22,340
and I don't know her.

204
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:23,800
So how do I approach her?

205
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,800
I heard she sometimes hangs out with Yuki.

206
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,740
So maybe he's my in.

207
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:30,480
I don't know her.

208
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:31,780
She doesn't know me.

209
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:34,040
This is gonna be tough.

210
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,720
Wait, how do you make friends with someone you don't know?

211
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:40,580
Easy.

212
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:42,240
Be honest and say something like,

213
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,700
Hey you, let's be friends.

214
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,380
That's never gonna work.

215
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:46,960
You're thinking that's never gonna work,

216
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:47,700
but it might.

217
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,160
Psychic witch.

218
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,000
I can't believe you're already looking for another girlfriend.

219
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:54,160
How do you know him?

220
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,420
I didn't, but I do now.

221
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:58,040
You're right.

222
00:11:58,140 --> 00:11:59,380
This person's a girl.

223
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:01,520
But I just wanna be her friend.

224
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:03,080
Well, if that's what you want,

225
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:04,300
then what's the harm in asking?

226
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:06,240
To get what you want in life,

227
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:07,440
you have to think positively.

228
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:09,240
You never know till you try.

229
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:15,020
I have to go somewhere really quick.

230
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:17,740
Is it cool if I meet you guys at the Children's Center?

231
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:18,720
Yeah, sure.

232
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:20,600
Okay, see you guys in a little bit.

233
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:21,080
Later.

234
00:12:21,820 --> 00:12:22,460
See ya!

235
00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:37,920
Looks like her class gets out at 6.30.

236
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:41,360
I can walk Hiromi home and be back here in time.

237
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:45,060
I have to get familiar with Aya's daily routine.

238
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:59,540
Aya pretty much kept to a straightforward schedule.

239
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,780
If someone wanted to kidnap her,

240
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:03,480
the best time would be right now,

241
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:05,300
after she got out of cram school.

242
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:07,540
Satoru!

243
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,320
I need your muscles.

244
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,760
Come on, shake a leg.

245
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:13,160
Why'd she have to show up now?

246
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,200
I'm trying to find out where Aya lives.

247
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:17,440
Why the heck'd you buy all this stuff?

248
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:18,160
Couldn't help it.

249
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:19,060
It was cheap.

250
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:20,280
It's heavy.

251
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:22,080
God, stop complaining.

252
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,600
It'll only make it heavier.

253
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,380
It'd be as heavy either way.

254
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:30,820
You're a lifesaver, sir.

255
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:32,980
Mom sort of went nuts at the store.

256
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:34,440
I did not go nuts.

257
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:42,800
So, Mr. Yoshiro,

258
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:44,920
how come you're not married?

259
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:46,740
That came out of nowhere.

260
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,900
It's like this.

261
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:52,780
Getting married depends on finding the right partner.

262
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:54,520
It depends on timing,

263
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,960
and whether they want to marry you,

264
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,620
and, well, other things.

265
00:13:58,520 --> 00:13:58,820
Me?

266
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,560
I already failed horribly at it once,

267
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,500
so I guess I'm just being extra cautious.

268
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:04,560
Sorry.

269
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,300
I didn't mean to...

270
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:08,220
It's okay.

271
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:10,100
It's all in the past now.

272
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:15,920
I was wondering if you could give me some advice.

273
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:20,060
How to approach a girl you don't know, huh?

274
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:21,240
Yeah.

275
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,580
I know a couple things about her, but that's it.

276
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:24,980
Let's see.

277
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:27,100
How would I go about doing that?

278
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,540
I guess I'd get her to drop her guard first.

279
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,040
That way I won't freak her out.

280
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,580
How do I do that?

281
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:32,980
Easy.

282
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:35,000
When you're around her, be yourself.

283
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:35,940
That's all.

284
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:37,300
Whatever you're into,

285
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,820
be it sports or cooking,

286
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:40,740
your interests make you interesting.

287
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:42,880
Your enthusiasm will make her curious,

288
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,400
and then she'll drop her guard.

289
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:45,560
Whoa.

290
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:47,640
I wish it were that impressive.

291
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,660
No, I'm bad at expressing my feelings directly,

292
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:52,640
so I've gotten good at relying on logic.

293
00:14:56,420 --> 00:14:57,720
What's this doing here?

294
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,080
No.

295
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:00,080
No, don't touch it!

296
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:02,640
I didn't mean to...

297
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:04,640
What the...

298
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:07,700
Well, my secret's out.

299
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:12,200
Candy?

300
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,320
There's no sense in hiding the truth anymore.

301
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:17,040
Don't just sit there.

302
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:18,340
Help me eat the evidence.

303
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:22,560
I quit smoking three years ago,

304
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:25,660
and candy's the only thing that helps stop the cravings.

305
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:27,720
I find someplace private,

306
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,280
jam a couple of these in my mouth,

307
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:29,820
and I'm good.

308
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:31,500
What a weirdo.

309
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,220
Thank you.

310
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:41,540
Can I bum one of those off you?

311
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:43,060
Sure.

312
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:50,620
I'm going over to the children's center to do my homework.

313
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:51,640
Okay.

314
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:54,540
Um, if you wait a sec, I'll go with you.

315
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:57,800
Are you gonna be Hiromi's bodyguard now that Kaio's gone?

316
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:58,940
It's not like that.

317
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:02,720
Satoru, can I talk to you for a sec?

318
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:03,920
Uh-huh.

319
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:06,500
Sorry.

320
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:08,480
I'll catch up in a few, okay?

321
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:09,200
Mm-hmm.

322
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:12,740
I have no idea what's going on with you lately.

323
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:16,020
You made it your mission to save Kaio, and you did,

324
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:17,200
so what's bothering you?

325
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:19,300
You always look so intense,

326
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:22,540
like you're still trying to fix whatever it is that needs fixing.

327
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,640
If something's bugging you,

328
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:26,300
I wish you'd just tell me about it.

329
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,620
I can't really explain what it is.

330
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:31,460
I'm still trying to figure it out.

331
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:35,580
Then, let me help you figure it out.

332
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:39,980
I'd like the chance to be a hero, too.

333
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:44,020
Whatever you're up to, I'd like to come along.

334
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:51,920
Check it out.

335
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:53,460
What do you think of these footprints?

336
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,340
A grown-up was here.

337
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:56,600
They came and left.

338
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:58,780
Yeah, but no tread.

339
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:00,860
It's like he wrapped his shoes in something.

340
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:01,680
Why?

341
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:03,100
They'd be super slippy.

342
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:05,560
Maybe to hide the tread pattern.

343
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:16,220
Look, the backpack's gone.

344
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:17,360
Crap.

345
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,980
Box with the stove, too.

346
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,360
Quite a few boxes are missing.

347
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,460
Andy tore some open.

348
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:26,700
He didn't want to leave any evidence behind.

349
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:30,820
Satoru, where are you going with this?

350
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:33,880
You guys remember what Kaio told us?

351
00:17:34,440 --> 00:17:37,160
That night she was here alone and she heard someone come in?

352
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:37,800
Yeah.

353
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,340
He left a backpack full of creepy junk.

354
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:41,220
So what?

355
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:44,220
I think that guy, whoever he is,

356
00:17:44,300 --> 00:17:46,380
is a serial killer who targets kids.

357
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:47,920
Wait, a serial killer?

358
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:49,140
You're joking.

359
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,380
No, I'm not.

360
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,860
I know it's hard to believe, but that's what I think.

361
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:56,760
Okay, but like, why?

362
00:17:56,760 --> 00:18:00,000
I wish I could explain it to you guys, but I can't.

363
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:03,440
When I saw the stuff from the backpack and the stove and charcoal,

364
00:18:03,780 --> 00:18:06,660
I thought maybe the killer was using this as their home base.

365
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:08,800
I know, guys.

366
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:11,640
Everything I just said to you sounds totally crazy.

367
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:14,100
But even so, I think I'm right.

368
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,520
As for Kaio, the truth is,

369
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:21,100
it wasn't just because her mom beat her that I didn't want to leave her alone.

370
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:23,780
I was also protecting her from the killer.

371
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:30,820
Geez, it's so out there,

372
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,800
it's like the plot of some detective story.

373
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:35,020
But the real issue here

374
00:18:35,020 --> 00:18:37,220
isn't whether we believe in your theory or not.

375
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:40,240
It's about whether we believe in you or not.

376
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:45,560
You don't have to walk me all the way home.

377
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:47,780
I can take care of myself, you know?

378
00:18:48,020 --> 00:18:50,240
I had to swing by here for something else anyway.

379
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:50,400
Okay.

380
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:57,780
Satoru?

381
00:18:59,140 --> 00:18:59,660
What?

382
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:02,700
I believe what you told us before.

383
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:05,300
And I'll do whatever I can to help out.

384
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,020
You can totally count on me.

385
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,280
You're the best.

386
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:10,840
See ya!

387
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:11,800
Night, Hiromi!

388
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:12,880
See you later!

389
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:20,320
I have to be honest here, Satoru.

390
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:21,860
After hearing your story,

391
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:24,280
I'm about 99% sure it's nonsense.

392
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:25,880
But still,

393
00:19:26,320 --> 00:19:29,040
there's a 1% chance everything you said's true.

394
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:31,600
Well, from your point of view,

395
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,440
I get how you think I'm making it up

396
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:34,880
and just playing detective and...

397
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,220
You should keep playing detective.

398
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:40,480
I don't know what that stuff we found here was for,

399
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,780
but you seem to really believe something's up,

400
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,760
and that makes me think that you might be onto something.

401
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:47,600
Mm-hmm.

402
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:51,140
Besides, you trusted us enough to tell us about it.

403
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:53,660
If you believe in us that much,

404
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:54,720
we believe in you.

405
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:56,880
If someone believes in you,

406
00:19:57,180 --> 00:19:57,980
you're not alone.

407
00:19:58,700 --> 00:20:00,400
And if I was in your situation,

408
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:02,080
I'd want someone to believe me.

409
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:05,820
Thank you, Kenya.

410
00:20:06,220 --> 00:20:07,320
You too, Hiromi.

411
00:20:10,320 --> 00:20:11,360
You don't get it.

412
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:12,460
I could have saved her.

413
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:14,440
18 years ago,

414
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:17,000
I was crying when I said that to my mom.

415
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,440
I don't want to feel that kind of guilt again.

416
00:20:22,940 --> 00:20:25,100
I'm the only one who can stop this.

417
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:27,260
The only one who can save them.

418
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,960
Remember to get your parents' signature.

419
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,620
Don't forget now.

420
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:41,300
I need you guys to come with me,

421
00:20:41,380 --> 00:20:42,420
but just us, okay?

422
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:45,780
Hey, Satoru,

423
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,680
today's a good day to go to the hideout.

424
00:20:48,260 --> 00:20:48,700
Actually,

425
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:50,440
we have to take care of something.

426
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:52,400
Sorry about that.

427
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:53,480
Yeah, sorry.

428
00:20:53,700 --> 00:20:54,060
That's cool.

429
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:55,060
See ya.

430
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:59,340
I wonder what the heck those dudes are up to.

431
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,560
They're acting weird.

432
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:01,540
Wanna follow them?

433
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:01,880
Mm-hmm.

434
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:02,900
Come on!

435
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:03,740
Right behind ya!

436
00:21:03,740 --> 00:21:08,400
I wonder what the heck those dudes are up to.

437
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,860
I wonder what the heck those dudes are up to.

438
00:21:09,860 --> 00:21:11,320
don't worry.

439
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:21,720
Oh, Jesus!

440
00:21:41,320 --> 00:22:11,300
Thank you.

441
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:41,300
Thank you.

442
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:43,320
Thank you.

